IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `uc-core`
IMPORT `uc2-part6-ch1-capital`

-- Tests of Part 6, Chapter 1 (regulations 45 to 50). Every expected value is worked out by hand from the text and written beside
-- the assertion; none is copied from the encoding's own output.

§ `Regulation 46 -- what is included in capital`

GIVEN possession IS A BOOLEAN
      regular IS A BOOLEAN
      instalments IS A BOOLEAN
      outstanding IS A NUMBER
      other IS A NUMBER
      disregarded IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Sum considered under regulation 46`
`test sum` possession regular instalments outstanding other disregarded MEANS
    `Sum considered under regulation 46` WITH
        `personal possession` IS possession
        `sum paid regularly and by reference to a period` IS regular
        `capital payable by instalments` IS instalments
        `amount of the capital outstanding` IS outstanding
        `other capital of the person and, if the person is a member of a couple, of the other member` IS other
        `capital to be disregarded under regulation 48` IS disregarded

-- (2) personal possessions are not capital, whatever else is true of them (src:853).
#ASSERT `reg 46 — how a sum is treated` (`test sum` TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE) EQUALS `not treated as capital because it is a personal possession`
#ASSERT `reg 46 — how a sum is treated` (`test sum` TRUE TRUE FALSE 0 0 TRUE) EQUALS `not treated as capital because it is a personal possession`
-- (3) a sum paid regularly and by reference to a period is income even if it would be capital (src:854).
#ASSERT `reg 46 — how a sum is treated` (`test sum` FALSE TRUE FALSE 0 0 FALSE) EQUALS `treated as income`
-- (1) other capital is taken into account unless disregarded (src:850-852).
#ASSERT `reg 46 — how a sum is treated` (`test sum` FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE) EQUALS `capital that is taken into account`
#ASSERT `reg 46 — how a sum is treated` (`test sum` FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 0 TRUE) EQUALS `capital that is disregarded`
-- (4) instalments: outstanding 10,000 and other capital 6,000 is exactly 16,000, which does not exceed 16,000: capital (src:855).
#ASSERT `reg 46 — how a sum is treated` (`test sum` FALSE FALSE TRUE 10000 6000 FALSE) EQUALS `capital that is taken into account`
-- One penny over: income.
#ASSERT `reg 46 — how a sum is treated` (`test sum` FALSE FALSE TRUE 10000 6000.01 FALSE) EQUALS `treated as income`
-- One penny under: capital.
#ASSERT `reg 46 — how a sum is treated` (`test sum` FALSE FALSE TRUE 10000 5999.99 FALSE) EQUALS `capital that is taken into account`
-- Instalments treated as capital can still be disregarded under (1)(b).
#ASSERT `reg 46 — how a sum is treated` (`test sum` FALSE FALSE TRUE 10000 5000 TRUE) EQUALS `capital that is disregarded`
-- (3) is "subject to paragraph (4)": instalments paid regularly are decided by (4), so 1,000 outstanding with nothing else is capital.
#ASSERT `reg 46 — how a sum is treated` (`test sum` FALSE TRUE TRUE 1000 0 FALSE) EQUALS `capital that is taken into account`
#ASSERT `reg 46 — how a sum is treated` (`test sum` FALSE TRUE TRUE 17000 0 FALSE) EQUALS `treated as income`

§ `Regulation 47 -- jointly held capital`

GIVEN whole IS A NUMBER
      persons IS A NUMBER
      evidence IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A `Jointly held capital asset`
`test joint asset` whole persons evidence MEANS
    `Jointly held capital asset` WITH
        `value of the whole of the beneficial interest` IS whole
        `number of persons with a beneficial interest, including the person` IS persons
        `fraction of the whole that the evidence to the contrary shows is the person's share` IS evidence

-- Equal shares in the absence of evidence to the contrary (src:857): 10,000 between two is 5,000; between three is 3,333.33.
#ASSERT `reg 47 — the value of the person's share of jointly held capital` (`test joint asset` 10000 2 NOTHING) EQUALS JUST 5000
#ASSERT `reg 47 — the value of the person's share of jointly held capital` (`test joint asset` 10000 3 NOTHING) EQUALS JUST 3333.33
-- With evidence that the share is a quarter: 2,500.
#ASSERT `reg 47 — the value of the person's share of jointly held capital` (`test joint asset` 10000 2 (JUST 0.25)) EQUALS JUST 2500
-- Nobody with an interest: the text does not answer.
#ASSERT `reg 47 — the value of the person's share of jointly held capital` (`test joint asset` 10000 0 NOTHING) EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Regulation 48 -- capital disregarded`

#ASSERT `reg 48(1) — the capital is disregarded` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 48(1) — the capital is disregarded` FALSE)
-- (2) the 6 months is extended only if the Secretary of State extends it, and never shortened.
#ASSERT (`reg 48(2) — the period that Schedule 10 specifies as 6 months` NOTHING)'s quantity EQUALS 6
#ASSERT (`reg 48(2) — the period that Schedule 10 specifies as 6 months` NOTHING)'s unit EQUALS months
#ASSERT (`reg 48(2) — the period that Schedule 10 specifies as 6 months` (JUST 9))'s quantity EQUALS 9
#ASSERT (`reg 48(2) — the period that Schedule 10 specifies as 6 months` (JUST 9))'s unit EQUALS months
#ASSERT (`reg 48(2) — the period that Schedule 10 specifies as 6 months` (JUST 4))'s quantity EQUALS 6

§ `Regulation 49 -- valuation of capital`

GIVEN value IS A NUMBER
      outside IS A BOOLEAN
      prohibition IS A BOOLEAN
      sale IS A NUMBER
      expenses IS A BOOLEAN
      encumbrances IS A NUMBER
      foreign IS A BOOLEAN
      charge IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Capital asset to be valued`
`test asset` value outside prohibition sale expenses encumbrances foreign charge MEANS
    `Capital asset to be valued` WITH
        `current market value or surrender value of the asset (in the country where it is possessed, in sterling terms)` IS value
        `possessed in a country outside the United Kingdom` IS outside
        `prohibition in that country against transferring an amount equal to the value to the United Kingdom` IS prohibition
        `amount it would raise if sold in the United Kingdom to a willing buyer` IS sale
        `there would be expenses attributable to sale` IS expenses
        `amount of any encumbrances secured on it` IS encumbrances
        `held in a currency other than sterling` IS foreign
        `banking charge or commission payable in converting it into sterling` IS charge

-- (1) market value 10,000: nothing to deduct leaves 10,000; expenses on sale take 10% (9,000); an encumbrance of 2,000 alone leaves 8,000; both leave 7,000.
#ASSERT `reg 49 — the value of capital` (`test asset` 10000 FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE 0 FALSE 0) EQUALS 10000
#ASSERT `reg 49 — the value of capital` (`test asset` 10000 FALSE FALSE 0 TRUE 0 FALSE 0) EQUALS 9000
#ASSERT `reg 49 — the value of capital` (`test asset` 10000 FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE 2000 FALSE 0) EQUALS 8000
#ASSERT `reg 49 — the value of capital` (`test asset` 10000 FALSE FALSE 0 TRUE 2000 FALSE 0) EQUALS 7000
-- (2) outside the United Kingdom, no prohibition: the market value in that country, 5,000; prohibition: what it would raise here, 3,000 (2,700 after the 10%).
#ASSERT `reg 49(2) — the market value of the asset` (`test asset` 5000 TRUE FALSE 3000 FALSE 0 FALSE 0) EQUALS 5000
#ASSERT `reg 49(2) — the market value of the asset` (`test asset` 5000 TRUE TRUE 3000 FALSE 0 FALSE 0) EQUALS 3000
#ASSERT `reg 49 — the value of capital` (`test asset` 5000 TRUE TRUE 3000 TRUE 0 FALSE 0) EQUALS 2700
-- A prohibition in a country where the asset is not possessed is irrelevant: an asset in the United Kingdom is worth its market value.
#ASSERT `reg 49(2) — the market value of the asset` (`test asset` 5000 FALSE TRUE 3000 FALSE 0 FALSE 0) EQUALS 5000
-- (3) a currency other than sterling: the banking charge of 50 comes off first (fork F-CAP2): 9,950; with sale expenses 9,950 less 995 is 8,955.
#ASSERT `reg 49 — the value of capital` (`test asset` 10000 FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE 0 TRUE 50) EQUALS 9950
#ASSERT `reg 49 — the value of capital` (`test asset` 10000 FALSE FALSE 0 TRUE 0 TRUE 50) EQUALS 8955
-- A charge on a sterling holding is not deducted.
#ASSERT `reg 49 — the value of capital` (`test asset` 10000 FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE 0 FALSE 50) EQUALS 10000
-- Rounding under regulation 6(1): 100.05 less 10.005 is 90.045, which rounds to 90.05.
#ASSERT `reg 49 — the value of capital` (`test asset` 100.05 FALSE FALSE 0 TRUE 0 FALSE 0) EQUALS 90.05
-- The text does not floor the value at nil: encumbrances of 1,500 on an asset of 1,000 give -500 (fork F-CAP2).
#ASSERT `reg 49 — the value of capital` (`test asset` 1000 FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE 1500 FALSE 0) EQUALS (0 MINUS 500)

§ `Regulation 50 -- notional capital`

GIVEN amount IS A NUMBER
      purpose IS A BOOLEAN
      debt IS A BOOLEAN
      purchase IS A BOOLEAN
      reasonable IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Disposal of capital considered under regulation 50`
`test disposal` amount purpose debt purchase reasonable MEANS
    `Disposal of capital considered under regulation 50` WITH
        `amount of the capital of which the person has deprived themselves` IS amount
        `deprived themselves of the capital for the purpose of securing entitlement to universal credit or to an increased amount of universal credit` IS purpose
        `disposed of it for the purpose of reducing or paying a debt owed by the person` IS debt
        `disposed of it for the purpose of purchasing goods or services` IS purchase
        `the expenditure was reasonable in the circumstances of the person's case` IS reasonable

-- (1) deprived for the purpose: treated as possessing 20,000.
#ASSERT `reg 50(1) — the person is treated as possessing the capital` (`test disposal` 20000 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `reg 50(1) — the notional capital` (`test disposal` 20000 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS 20000
-- Not for that purpose: not treated, and no notional capital.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 50(1) — the person is treated as possessing the capital` (`test disposal` 20000 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE))
#ASSERT `reg 50(1) — the notional capital` (`test disposal` 20000 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS 0
-- (2)(a) paying a debt: not depriving (src:872).
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 50(1) — the person is treated as possessing the capital` (`test disposal` 20000 TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE))
-- (2)(b) purchasing goods or services where the expenditure was reasonable: not depriving (src:873).
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 50(1) — the person is treated as possessing the capital` (`test disposal` 20000 TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE))
-- A purchase that was not reasonable does not escape; reasonableness without a purchase is irrelevant.
#ASSERT `reg 50(1) — the person is treated as possessing the capital` (`test disposal` 20000 TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT `reg 50(1) — the person is treated as possessing the capital` (`test disposal` 20000 TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE)

-- (3)(a) over 16,000: reduced by the award the Secretary of State considers would be made. 20,000 less 300 is 19,700.
#ASSERT `reg 50(3) — the notional capital after an assessment period or month` 20000 300 EQUALS 19700
-- 16,000.01 is over 16,000: less 100 is 15,900.01.
#ASSERT `reg 50(3) — the notional capital after an assessment period or month` 16000.01 100 EQUALS 15900.01
-- (3)(b) exactly 16,000 is not over 16,000: reduced by the regulation 72 yield, 40 x 4.35 = 174: 15,826.
#ASSERT `reg 50(3) — the notional capital after an assessment period or month` 16000 300 EQUALS 15826
-- 10,000: yield 16 x 4.35 = 69.60; 9,930.40.
#ASSERT `reg 50(3) — the notional capital after an assessment period or month` 10000 300 EQUALS 9930.4
-- 6,001: yield 4.35: 5,996.65.
#ASSERT `reg 50(3) — the notional capital after an assessment period or month` 6001 300 EQUALS 5996.65
-- 6,000 and under: no reduction is provided (fork F-CAP3).
#ASSERT `reg 50(3) — the notional capital after an assessment period or month` 6000 300 EQUALS 6000
#ASSERT `reg 50(3) — the notional capital after an assessment period or month` 5000 300 EQUALS 5000
